Ideas learned from these MIT-licensed projects. No code or text was copied.

- tribunal (https://github.com/kdoubt/tribunal): claims with a state, dissent kept on the record, and
  publishing one's own null results.
- autodecision (https://github.com/harshilmathur/autodecision): a decision journal kept for later
  comparison with outcomes.
- futureos (https://github.com/DresdenGman/futureos): forecast before acting, and score it.
- cc-thinking-skills (https://github.com/tjboudreaux/cc-thinking-skills): matching the depth of work
  to how reversible a choice is.

The studies behind each step are cited in skills/judgement-decide/references/evidence.md.
